V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:5:## A. Information interfaces (declared, equalised across arms)
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:7:A2. **I_coordinator** (per anchor): global nominal geometry with beam-specific cross gains, all users' legal sets, b⁻, the reference proposal a⁰, the bounded catalogue 𝒞 (decision 4/CB-2), the nominal model 𝓜 (no realised fading, no future TLE beyond the declared forecast horizon), and the outputs of 𝓜 for each profile in 𝒞 (joint load, coupled powers, interference, activation, service, bits, energy, continuation). Compute = the declared budget (§F).
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:9:A4. **Equalised between FULL and every DROP/comparator arm:** primitive access and timestamps, forecast method, physical identities, catalogue construction (authenticated identical catalogues at matched anchors), joint search, guards, tie-breaking, validation, deadline, fallback. Any learned pruning is part of the declared intervention. An exact evaluator may never reinsert a removed score through ranking, pruning or a score-dependent guard.
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:16:B5. **C3 training rows** carry the complete coalition context: anchor, a⁰, the changed-user set A, their selected actions a_A, the global resource context (occupancy, activation, shared capacity, interference summary per affected beam), and the label Ψ_A / κ. Coalition size for label computation is capped at |A| ≤ 4 (2^|A| subset evaluations bounded); larger evacuation sets are labelled by the capped decomposition and flagged. Per-user Shapley credit is reporting only (pairs: Ψ/2 each), never a training target.
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:18:## C. Stage 7 — learner, arms, deployment
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:20:C2. **C3 learner form:** a **set-conditioned scalar interaction head** Ψ̂_θ(Z_t, a⁰, A, a_A): permutation-invariant over A, anchored Ψ̂(∅) = Ψ̂({u}) = 0, trained on the residual Ψ_A / κ over the coalition support of the bounded catalogue; deployed S3 optimises the **complete** score C1 + C2 + Ψ̂ over 𝒞 with the sealed service guard, budget and fallback. S0 = the same selector with the exact Ψ_A in place of Ψ̂. S_UNI = iterated exact unilateral improvement to a local optimum (every legal unilateral alternative evaluated with the same nominal joint physics at each iterate, deterministic improving move, atomic commit of the final profile only, termination certificate reported).
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:22:C4. **Coordination attribution (beyond the source claim):** FULL (S3) > DROP_C3 **and** FULL > the S_UNI-equipped comparator on held-out realised pooled EE, QoS margins met, plus decision-relevant nonadditivity (the selected profile differs from the additive/unilateral optimum at a reported fraction of anchors, including rejected harmful joint moves) — the requirement "g_I ≠ 0" is withdrawn. **Learned value (S3 vs matched S0)** is one predeclared axis: realised closed-loop pooled EE under equal computation budget including timeouts; matching S0 at lower compute is an acceleration claim, reported separately.
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:23:C5. **Neutral sources** sealed before generation: generator, labels, support, strata, overlap, row weights, optimisation dose; "identical batches across arms" means identical within a route/source identity; every DROP checkpoint retains all heads, the neutral-trained head differs from initialisation and participates in deployment (KATs).
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:24:C6. **Zero results are allowed and informative:** a zero C3 source marginal ends the positive C3 claim under this scope; an interval excluding the practical margin supports "no practically relevant benefit"; a lower-bound failure alone is inconclusive; neither permits changing features, catalogues, sources or regimes until C3 becomes positive.
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:25:C7. **Epochs, checkpoints, seeds:** deterministic aggregate epochs with sealed row counts/order/digests; checkpoints every 100 source epochs with `completed_source_epochs` and batch digests; **12 learner seeds** (§E), each lineage sharing one serialised initialisation and identical source batches per route identity across arms; `learner_seed` and `world_seed` separate everywhere.
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:27:## D. Stage 8 — panel, statistics, harness
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:28:D1. **Panel:** 6 arms × 12 learner seeds × 2 worlds per TRAIN date over the ≈ 160 claim dates (≈ 320 worlds per arm-seed; ≈ 30 steps per world), allocation manifest sealed with role-wise date disjointness (claim dates unused by any successor development activity; legacy overlap recorded); no TEST.
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:29:D2. **Estimator:** pooled ΣB/ΣE; primary interval = two-way pigeonhole bootstrap over dates × learner seeds with arms paired within resamples and the ratio recomputed per draw (central 95 % percentile); one-way cluster bootstrap and delta-method supplementary; seedwise paired effects reported; δ = +0.5 % relative with the 2.5th-percentile lower bound (v1.4); QoS margins with additive numerators/denominators inside draws (stage-2 decision 6, item 37).
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:32:D5. **Harness:** attempt registry (STARTED before outcomes), canonical per-step receipts, merge re-aggregation from rows, conformance suite (NULL ≡ BASE per step, real-step dry-run of every arm, write-once sha256 receipts, authority manifest), same physics/endpoint digest as training, one terminal adjudication.
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:35:Planning alternative Δ* = +2 % relative (both reviewers: a true +1 % is not detectable with ≈ 160 dates under any seed count if the date SD is ≈ 5 %). Variance sensitivities: date SD 3 / 5 / 10 %, seed SD 1 / 2 %. With date SD 5 %, seed SD 1 %, 160 dates, 12 seeds and negligible residual variance, the per-contrast one-sided power at the 2.5 % level is ≈ 0.86 (SE ≈ 0.49 %); the three-contrast conjunction ≈ 0.64 if independent. With 5 seeds it is ≈ 0.70 / 0.34. 12 seeds is the declared design; the date component caps further gains. The crossed-cluster inference test (§G T3) calibrates the actual procedure at 5 and 12 seeds before any real evaluation.
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:40:F3. **Capability manifest fields:** telemetry sources and ages, roster and cross-gain coverage, model assumptions and calibration source, worker hardware/count, catalogue bounds, solver limits, memory, missing-data handling, measured end-to-end latency distribution.
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:45:T3 **Crossed-cluster inference through the real merger:** synthetic raw receipts with controlled date/seed/world effects for the 3/5/10 % SD scenarios, repeated worlds per cell, unequal energies (pooled ≠ mean EE), identical arms, zero-bit and undefined-denominator cells, injected alternatives, least-favourable conjunction null (one component at the +0.5 % boundary); verify pairing, interval calibration, conjunction power and QoS rejection at 5 and 12 seeds.
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v0-2026-09-08.md:6:1. **Producer:** tapes (provider decisions 9–11) → per (anchor, user, legal action) rows built by one production builder; every row carries world/user/action/time/calibration lineage; TRAIN-only asserted at construction.
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v0-2026-09-08.md:9:4. **Labels:** C1 whole-network surplus + Φ (bits / κ); C2 three-offset forecast core with −κ per absorbing lost offset (bits / κ); C3 interaction share only (Ψ/2 pairs; Shapley for sets) over the sealed bounded catalogue; κ per stage-4 item 24; all prices explicit.
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v0-2026-09-08.md:15:8. **Seeds and CRN:** five learner seeds (v1.0 evaluation design governs over the round-3 "three initializations"), each lineage sharing one serialised initialisation and identical source batches across arms; `learner_seed` and `world_seed` are separate fields everywhere.
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v0-2026-09-08.md:16:9. **Deployed selector:** per-user masked argmax of the normalised Q1 + Q2 sum (bits / κ) for the two-head policy; the C3 layer is the set-level coordinator (learned S3 or exact S0) over the bounded catalogue with the sealed service guard, a 30.08 s deadline, BASE-proposal fallback, and the deployment-capability manifest (stage-4 item 26); the information-matched `S_UNI` comparator is always evaluated beside it.
V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v0-2026-09-08.md:20:11. **Panel:** the sealed design (6 arms × 5 learner seeds × ≈ 600 TRAIN worlds over ≈ 161 dates; ≈ 30 steps per world) with a prospective allocation manifest (decision CD-6); cluster = TLE date × learner seed; no TEST split.
V025-PILOT-TRACK-DECLARATION-2026-09-09.md:7:**Scope:** quarantined development worlds only (`V025_PROBE/world/{1,2}` for training rows, `world/{3,4}` for evaluation), the engine as it stands at the stage-4d/4f snapshot with the fixed provider, 30 anchors per world per carrier, the sealed catalogue and arms, **4 learner seeds** and the sealed learner configuration, 6 arms.
V025-PILOT-TRACK-DECLARATION-2026-09-09.md:9:**Binding limits:** pilot numbers may never enter the paper, may never select a configuration, a regime, a margin, a seed count or any sealed rule, and may never be cited as evidence for or against C1, C2 or C3. Their only admissible uses are (i) finding integration and engineering defects, (ii) measuring cost, (iii) deciding *engineering* priorities. The pilot cannot trigger PHYSICS-GO and cannot substitute for the a-r0 matrix.
V025-PILOT-TRACK-DECLARATION-2026-09-09.md:13:Stage 4g → its audit → seal package → a-r0 matrix → admission trichotomy → PHYSICS-GO → confirmatory source generation and training on the claim panel with 16 seeds. Nothing in Track F alters this sequence, its worlds, its seeds or its rules.
V025-PILOT-TRACK-DECLARATION-2026-09-09.md:16:The pilot worlds are already quarantined from the claim panel (world 1 was opened before sealing; the formal panel uses the `V025_PROBE_R2` / `V025_CAL_R2` namespaces and reserved claim dates). The pilot uses the same code as Track S, so every integration defect it finds is a real defect of the confirmatory path, found earlier and more cheaply.
C1C2-ENCODER-REPAIR-2026-09-10.md:7:No learner training or production run was performed. No threshold, sign, seed, horizon, price, service guard, acceptance rule, or `PILOT_PRIMITIVE_SOURCE_FALLBACK` was changed. The sealed clone and its virtual environment were not modified; its Python executable was used read-only with `PYTHONPATH=src` and `nice -n 15`.
C1C2-ENCODER-REPAIR-2026-09-10.md:15:- `_build_anchor_rows_primitive` defines survival as `future_metric["legal"] and identity is not None`, then writes that same value to both `valid` and `survival` (`scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:416-430`). `_primitive_metrics` defines `legal` only from future visibility, D2 eligibility, and cell reachability (`scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:323-352`). It never asks whether the coupled evaluator serves the user.
C1C2-ENCODER-REPAIR-2026-09-10.md:19:For the real witness, both anchors have the same physical step-0 tape, current base mapping, incumbent mapping, and focal candidate `(user=6, action=(65028,44))`. Nevertheless, the future carrier transition makes the target predicate range over 93 changed users at each offset for anchor 0, but only the focal user for anchor 1. Thus the target uses the same predicate on different `changed` inputs across anchors, while the primitive encoder uses an entirely different predicate.
C1C2-ENCODER-REPAIR-2026-09-10.md:26:The absorbing rule is applied to the target but not to the encoded row. `c2_persistence_forecast` maintains `alive`; a first invalid/non-surviving projection makes every later offset a loss (`src/mcrl/physics_v025/targets.py:289-310`). Q2 stores three independent supplied booleans and has no cumulative `alive` transform. In this witness the distinction begins at offset 1, so anchor 0 incurs all three losses.
C1C2-ENCODER-REPAIR-2026-09-10.md:33:Across the two cheap anchors, 822 of 1,784 valid nonreference rows have at least one stored-vs-exact **survival** mismatch (792/892 at anchor 0 and 30/892 at anchor 1), totalling 2,406 offset flags. Additionally, 200 rows have validity mismatches (600 offset flags). Counting a row affected by either boolean gives 1,022/1,784 rows. These anchors contain the previously established 62 exact C2 collision groups.
C1C2-ENCODER-REPAIR-2026-09-10.md:52:| C2 | **No feature exists under the constraint** | Any deterministic function of decision-time state plus `(user 6,(65028,44))` receives identical inputs in both anchors. | Identical current tape/mapping/incumbent and candidate action. | Adding carrier identity, the future transition's changed-user set, or `_batched_stage2_forecasts(...).survives` is **inadmissible**: the first is source-policy context rather than network state, and the latter two use future/candidate coupled information. | Breaks neither; the admissible set remains empty. The tempting exact flag would give `(0,0,0)` vs `(1,1,1)`, but it is explicitly rejected as non-deployable. |
C1C2-ENCODER-REPAIR-2026-09-10.md:58:The rerun used `scripts/diagnose_v025_c1c2_sufficiency.py --anchors 30`, seed `20260909`, and the same physical-step split: train `1,2,4,6,7,8,9`; validation `5`; test `0,3`. It retained 26,345 exact-relabelled nonreference rows; the test set has 5,280 rows. Each deployable row used standardized inverse-distance k-NN with `k` selected from `{1,3,7,15,31}` on validation; `k=31` was selected throughout.
C1C2-ENCODER-REPAIR-2026-09-10.md:69:The admissible C1 repair buys **no measured predictive power**. Its value is exactly `1.0` at all 30 corpus anchors because every current base configuration reaches the RF cap, so standardization removes it. This negative result is not evidence that the feature is wrongly chosen for identifiability; it shows that breaking one contract witness does not supply variation useful on this corpus. C2 is unchanged because no admissible separator exists.
C1C2-ENCODER-REPAIR-2026-09-10.md:79:C2 also cannot presently be expected to raise pooled energy efficiency. Although Q2's held-out EV is positive (`0.2107`), its stored survival semantics are wrong on 822/1,784 two-anchor rows, and the exact target varies with future carrier-transition context absent from admissible deployment inputs. Correcting offline flags by copying coupled forecast outcomes would be leakage, not a deployable encoder repair. Before any efficacy claim, the focal-survival target must be made a function of admissible decision-time information (or the per-user C2 head design reconsidered), then evaluated on a fresh untouched split. No pooled-EE conclusion follows here.
MATCHED-ANCHOR-TIER-2026-09-10.md:1:The shared-catalogue lookup is sound for the implemented fixed-reference pilot; it is not a verified full-source tier, and per-arm learned seeds can break sharing for DROP_C1, DROP_C2 and all three single-informative arms.
