V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:85:The C2 tie-break diagnostic is the fraction of non-incumbent (user, action) candidates whose C2 head score is exactly equal to the incumbent's under the FULL arm, i.e. C2 cannot discriminate the move and the ranking falls through to C1 plus the stable configuration-ID tie-break. `c2_tie_frequency` is the fraction of anchor-seed decisions with any such tie; `c2_tie_pair_fraction_mean` is the mean per-decision tie fraction. See DEFECTS.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:96:PILOT_NOT_CLAIM. **Only the `evaluation` row was produced by this minimal run.** The `rows` and `training` rows are the inherited full-scale phase manifests (2 worlds x 90 anchors; 4 seeds x 5 learned arms x 2000 epochs) and are reported for cost context only.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:110:- **D-MIN-2 (suspicious result, unexplained). `S_UNI` is exactly degenerate with `BASELINE`.** Pooled EE for `S_UNI` equals `BASELINE` to the last digit (16 987 632 bits/J) at every one of the 5 anchors. Under the 5 s pilot `compute_budget_s`, `_s_uni_select` returned the carrier base unchanged, i.e. it found no accepted unilateral improvement at all. The `FULL-vs-S_UNI` contrast below is therefore **not** a comparison against exhaustive unilateral improvement; per contract v1.2 item 6 it is at best a budget-limited operational comparator, and in this run it is an empty one. Do not read it as evidence.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:111:- **D-MIN-3 (suspicious result). `FULL` selects the all-users coalition (size 100) at every anchor-seed.** `escape_and_harm_by_coalition_size` shows `selected: 10` at size 100 and `selected: 0` at every size 2-6, while positive-joint escape opportunities exist at sizes 2-6. A selector that always moves all 100 users is far more likely to be an artefact of the epoch-200 head's scale than a real decision. Two of those ten selections were harmful by exact joint delta (harmful-acceptance rate 0.2).
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:112:- **D-MIN-4 (internal inconsistency). `V_CA` is large and negative while `FULL` pooled EE is the highest of all arms.** Net `V_CA` is -1.365e11 bit-equivalents (bits -1.222e10, -eta*energy -3.373e10, Phi -9.054e10) against the additive selector, yet `FULL` pooled EE (3.425e7) exceeds `DROP_C3` (2.352e7), `S0` (1.759e7) and `BASELINE` (1.699e7). Either the `V_CA` reference (the additive selector) or the pooled-EE aggregation is not measuring what the schema intends. **This must be resolved before any V_CA number is reported at scale.**
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:113:- **D-MIN-5 (now measured, previously zero-by-construction). C2 tie frequency.** The build-3 code had no C2 tie-break and the field was hard-coded `False`. This pilot implemented the smallest schema-satisfying measurement: the fraction of non-incumbent (user, action) candidates whose FULL-arm C2 head score exactly equals the incumbent's. Measured value: **0.0** on both catalogue anchors (`c2_tie_frequency` 0.0, `c2_tie_pair_fraction_mean` 0.0). The C2 head discriminates every candidate; the zero is now an observation rather than an artefact, but it is still a proxy for head indiscriminability, not for a build-3 tie-break code path.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:115:- **D-MIN-7 (scope). Statistical power is nil.** 5 anchors x 1 carrier x 2 learner seeds = 10 FULL decisions per catalogue anchor. No interval, no seed-variance estimate and no contrast in this report is powered. The g_A/g_I quantiles below are computed over 10 points and p05/p95 coincide with min/max.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:117:- **D-MIN-9 (schema shortcut). `top_choice_agreement` differs sharply by catalogue anchor** (0.5 on `P-a0`, 0.0 on `P-u`) with no obvious mechanism at this sample size; recorded so it is checked, not explained.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:125:- No signed formal calibration manifest was present because stage 4d stopped on HOLD. The pilot uses an explicitly labelled one-development-anchor proxy solely to complete wiring; every row carries its exact values.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:133:- Exact S0 over 48 boundaries for every catalogue profile was unbounded in the joined engine. The pilot ranks S0's top-two proposals with provider-primitive C1+C2, applies the same bounded evacuation rule, evaluates that set with exact nominal boundary-0 physics, then evaluates the committed S0 profile over all 48 realised boundaries.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:134:- Exhaustive exact interaction decomposition over every catalogue row was also unbounded. Exact Psi is computed for every P-u joint escape candidate and every selected FULL coalition; other rows retain learned scoring only. P-u top-10 users are primitive-ranked by |d_i^u|. The pilot S_UNI wall budget was reduced to 5 seconds, with the engine's fallback and termination certificate retained verbatim.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:140:**PILOT_NOT_CLAIM.** Per `V025-PILOT-TRACK-DECLARATION-2026-09-09.md`, nothing in this report may enter the paper, select a configuration/regime/margin/seed count, or be cited for or against C1, C2 or C3. Its only admissible uses are integration-defect discovery, cost measurement, and engineering prioritisation.

